 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38829" :question/id #uuid "0823f14a-58fd-5bcb-8d22-3fa3daf4ef45" :question/math-academy-id "q-38829" :question/problem "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{3-x}{{x}^{2}-3x}$ is continuous." :question/worked-solution "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3-x}{{x}^{2}-3x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-x}{x(x-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 3.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ $(0,3),$ and $(3,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38829/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eac988ba-ea97-52c7-90a7-d451ee7f49e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76069/selection/a9017d134c27800a17b18aaae670d577a2e3f4a97b0795dc846f33e00896fab1" :answer/id #uuid "63ace388-eb2b-53b3-9060-02a69d1f8b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76069/selection/a5e9c9827d747d27532013ef10f8d9194070fe5db43f57f45a85449a31f32289" :answer/id #uuid "47707dd2-a711-5f88-8cfc-92415bd6484b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,4)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76069/selection/f4130f6d248e4139b05f3d7ac6a45cedb7b1d38703aad5c6a7a1fdc9cb040816" :answer/id #uuid "f2851b1e-d0e5-59f4-96f6-c87e75506e18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76069/selection/66082c2d2c80