consists of all real numbers $x$ such that $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ The largest subset of $I$ on which the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is continuous is\n\n$\\,[\\frac{\\pi }{2},$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃($\n{{field-2}}\n$,$\n{{field-3}}$].$" :question/worked-solution "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is continuous over the entire interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}],$ but the function $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is not defined at $x=\\pi .$ \n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ),$ and $(\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}],$ namely\n\n$$\n[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi )\\cup (\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340088/field-1" "q-340088/field-2" "q-340088/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340088"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
